## Twig ([Twig coding standards](https://twig.symfony.com/doc/3.x/coding_standards.html))

> **Examples:** `../examples/twig/style.examples.html.twig`

Syntax and expression formatting only — HTML document rules live in **HTML in Twig templates** (`html-in-twig.mdc`).

- Put exactly one space after `{{`, `{%`, `{#` and before `}}`, `%}`, `#}` when content is non-empty; with whitespace control (`-`), attach it directly to the delimiter (`{{- user -}}`, `{%- if user -%}`).
- Put exactly one space before and after comparison (`==`, `!=`, `<`, `>`, `>=`, `<=`), math (`+`, `-`, `/`, `*`, `%`, `//`, `**`), logic (`not`, `and`, `or`), `~`, `is`, `in`, and ternary (`?:`) operators.
- Put exactly one space after `:` in mappings and after `,` in sequences and mappings; no spaces inside `[...]`, `{...}`, or around `|`, `.`, `..`, `[]`.
- No spaces after `(` or before `)` in expressions; no spaces around string quotes; no spaces around filter/function call parentheses (`name|default('Fabien')`, `range(1..10)`).
- Put exactly one space before and after `=` in macro argument declarations (`{% macro html_input(class = "input") %}`).
- Use `:` (not `=`) to separate named argument names and values (`html_input(class: 'pwd')`, `convert_encoding(from: 'UTF-8', to: 'UTF-8')`); put one space after `:` in named arguments.
- Use snake_case for Twig template names, directories, and variable names (application-provided and template-created), filter/function/test names, macro argument names, and named arguments; prefix partial templates with `_` — flag PascalCase paths such as `catalog/ProductTile.html.twig`.
- Indent Twig tags and the HTML they emit consistently; match nesting depth in the rendered output.
- When the same field row, card layout, or table column block appears in multiple templates, use `{% include %}`, `{% embed %}`, `<twig:…>`, or a macro — do not copy-paste markup that differs only by variable names or labels.
